xping (1.4.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Exit codes for scripts and monitoring: 0 when a check passes, 1 when
    it fails, 2 for invalid usage, 130 on Ctrl-C.
  * Thresholds: ping/mtr --max-loss/--max-latency, tcp/http --max-latency,
    http --expect-status, tls --min-days, health/dnscheck --min-score;
    -q/--quiet for exit-code-only output.
  * IPv6: IPv6-only hosts work; -4/-6 force an address family.
  * ping, trace, mtr and health no longer need root on Linux: they use
    unprivileged ICMP sockets (IP_RECVERR for traceroute replies).
  * New commands: net (local network overview), propagation (compare a
    DNS record across public resolvers), check (batch checks from a
    TOML/JSON file with one exit code).
  * trace/mtr --asn show each hop's network operator (Team Cymru DNS).
  * tcp/http/health --watch and --until-up.
  * speedtest uses 4 parallel connections by default (-c, -d).
  * --csv/--markdown export real tables (one row per reply, hop, port,
    record, ...). JSON output is unchanged.
  * Fixes: unreadable ~/.xping no longer crashes commands; parallel
    health runs cannot corrupt the history file; man page corrections.

 -- Mehdi Askari <iorganamis@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xping (1.3.8-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Security: all TLS/HTTPS connections (tls, http, whois RDAP,
    speedtest) share one context that verifies certificates and
    requires TLS 1.2 or newer; whois no longer retries RDAP with
    certificate verification disabled.
  * http: fixed failures on HTTP/2-capable HTTPS sites (request now
    negotiates HTTP/1.1 only; HTTP/2 support probed separately).
  * dnscheck: DMARC read from _dmarc.<domain>; DKIM probed at common
    selectors; DNS query failures no longer reported as missing records.
  * listen: works on macOS; fixed Linux/Windows netstat parsing.
  * Export (--json/--csv/--markdown) now includes http timing fields,
    health history and the TLS certificate chain.
  * trace honours the IPv4 header length and passes --timeout to the
    system traceroute/tracert fallback; tcp connects to the resolved IP.
  * ping --watch rejects export flags instead of ignoring them;
    osdetect no longer crashes on unusual TTL values.
  * speedtest and osdetect accept --json/--csv/--markdown.

 -- Mehdi Askari <iorganamis@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0000

xping (1.3.7-1) noble; urgency=low

  * cli/main.py: the ASCII-art banner now prints only when `xping` is
    run with no arguments at all. It no longer prints before the
    bare-host shorthand (`xping 8.8.8.8`) or before any explicit
    subcommand (`xping ping ...`, `xping trace ...`, etc.) — every
    real command's output now starts immediately with its own result,
    not the banner first.

